132	        // Fits an independent least-squares line (position vs. time) through the
133	        // buffered samples for each axis, seeds the filter's state directly from
134	        // the fit's velocity (slope) and its position at the last sample's time
135	        // (evaluating the fit there, rather than trusting that one raw noisy
136	        // measurement, smooths noise on the position estimate too) — then commits
137	        // it as the filter's current belief with no extra Predict() step, same
138	        // reasoning as the two-point version this replaced: the fit already
139	        // represents the state AT the last sample's timestamp, so advancing it
140	        // again would overshoot.
