// comes nowhere near bridging, so the shot got cut off with only ~2 real ticks
// and an under-converged, LOW speed reading (15.5 m/s instead of the true 18).
// 17.5 degrees stays comfortably clear of that exit threshold for this whole
// trajectory (same margin the working 14-degree shot had), while still roughly
// doubling the ball's height at the goal line versus 14 degrees.
mock.SetTrajectory(speedMps: 18f, launchAngleDeg: 17.5f, azimuthDeg: 15f);

